    'Endometriosis is the presence of endometrial-like tissue outside the uterus, commonly on the ovaries (endometriomas), uterosacral ligaments, pouch of Douglas and pelvic peritoneum, causing cyclical pelvic pain, dysmenorrhoea, deep dyspareunia, dyschezia and subfertility, with tender nodularity and a fixed uterus on examination. Transvaginal ultrasound and MRI detect endometriomas and deep disease, but laparoscopy with histological confirmation remains the definitive diagnosis; CA-125 may be raised but is non-specific. Treatment is analgesia with NSAIDs, hormonal suppression (combined pills, progestogens, levonorgestrel intrauterine system, GnRH analogues with add-back) and surgical excision or ablation; fertility management may need assisted reproduction.',
